Stabilize: main scene boots clean headless, smoke failures cut from 30+ down to 7 (pre-kit expectations)

After the wave-agent edits to the 4 files and my StrReplace additions to player_class.gd, the
project wouldn't boot — autoloads failed with a circular parse chain, PlayerProfile was
missing kit surface, and main.gd's rift-clash hooks referenced stubs that didn't exist.
Now:

- PlayerClass script parses clean (removed duplicated kit_ability_ids/kit_for)
- PlayerProfile grew ability kit + meta surface: loadout_for, ability_pool_for,
  is_ult_unlocked (returns true), bank_wave_progress, sparks_for_wave — the wave agent
  already had save_audio_prefs+ability_kit wiring so those leaked through cleanly
- GameRuntime exposes is_rift_clash() returning false until team mode is loaded
- Arena got crater_unlocked/set_crater_unlocked stub so boss-crater unlock hook compiles
- VoiceService re-registered as autoload (deleted too aggressively last pass)
- player.gd: loadout typed Array[String], hazard_update no-op'd until lava push lands
- main.gd: Int/String coercions on rift-clash hooks, Dict type on bank_wave_progress,
  show_game_over() arg dropped, landmark iterate gated on Arena.landmarks existing,
  last_spawn_team assignment removed (Enemy has no team_id field)

Boot flow now: bootstrap boots silently; main boots silently (Steam thread warning unchanged);
class smoke test goes from 30+ failures to 7 — all are pre-kit-system expectations vs the
kit-default behavior (e.g. "fresh player should know no abilities") and can be reconciled
when the balance/two-press agents re-run on top of this stable baseline.
